// Title: Uncommon Extension Shim Database Installation Via Sdbinst.EXE
// Sigma ID: 18ee686c-38a3-4f65-9f44-48a077141f42
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-01 | Modified: 2024-01-10
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546.011
// Description: Detects installation of a potentially suspicious new shim with an uncommon extension using
//   sdbinst.exe. Adversaries may establish persistence and/or elevate privileges by executing
//   malicious content triggered by application shims
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/05/fin7-shim-databases-persistence.html
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20240115015113/https://github.com/nasbench/Misc-Research/blob/8ee690e43a379cbce8c9d61107442c36bd9be3d3/Other/Undocumented-Flags-Sdbinst.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d7c9da10c170a6988d68ebdf2c9f7bd8782b7c55/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sdbinst_susp_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\sdbinst.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "sdbinst.exe") and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains ".sdb" or ((ProcessCommandLine endswith " -c" or ProcessCommandLine endswith " -f" or ProcessCommandLine endswith " -mm" or ProcessCommandLine endswith " -t") or ProcessCommandLine contains " -m -bg") or isnull(ProcessCommandLine) or ProcessCommandLine =~ "")))
